# Intentionally committed (see the !frontend/.env exception in the root
# .gitignore). This holds only the public backend URL — the same non-secret
# value already committed in eas.json's build.<profile>.env blocks, and it
# ends up inlined into every shipped JS bundle regardless of where it comes
# from, so there is nothing to keep private here.
#
# Why this file has to exist at all: `eas build` reads EXPO_PUBLIC_* from
# eas.json's own env block, but `eas update` (OTA) does not — it runs
# `expo export` locally and reads EXPO_PUBLIC_* the normal Expo CLI way, from
# this file / the shell environment, at the moment someone runs the publish.
# Before this file existed, that meant the URL an OTA update baked in
# depended on whatever (if anything) was in an *untracked*, developer-local
# .env at publish time — invisible in git, easy to have missing or stale on
# a second machine, and the exact mechanism that has already caused OTA
# updates to ship with the wrong (or undefined) backend URL while eas.json
# itself was correct. Committing it removes that machine-dependent step.
#
# If this URL ever changes, update it here AND in eas.json's three build
# profiles together — they must always match.
EXPO_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=https://kabadi-market-backend.onrender.com
